NAME
    echo - print the arguments

SYNOPSIS
    echo [text]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the rest of the command line as the shell passed it (the
    spaces after the command word are dropped, everything else is
    kept) and a line feed. Nothing is interpreted: no quotes, escapes,
    variables or globs. echo is /BIN/ECHO.

LIMITS
    The argument tail is 127 characters.

EXAMPLES
    echo hello world        hello world
    echo *.TXT              *.TXT (globs are each command's business)

NOTES
    Y1/OS has no output redirection yet, so echo cannot write a file.
    New in Y1/OS 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    run, help
